<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Multi-task unified IR<span id="S3.T2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (<span id="S3.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Setting B</span>) comparison. </span>Best<span id="S3.T2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> and <span id="S3.T2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">second best</span> performances are highlighted.
Compared to state-of-the-art methods, our method has significant improvements in both fidelity and perception indicators. At the same time, extending our solution to the existing advanced restoration networks NAFNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> and X-Restormer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> can further improve the model performance.
</span></span></figcaption>
